# There is no `void` type keyword -- `void` is the implicit no-return
# (01-lexical.md:116-117, :307; appendix-b-keywords.md:18-20 lists the type
# keywords and `void` is not among them). `void` is ALSO tychoc0's internal
# spelling of the no-return type, so tychoc0 used to hand a written `void`
# annotation straight back as the real type and ACCEPT this program while tychoc
# rejected it -- the same fail-open accept/reject divergence as reject/str_as_type.ty,
# funnelling through the same internal-spelling guard in parse_type_d.
# Both compilers must reject.
fn f(x: void) -> void:
    return x

fn main():
    println("ok")
